":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York, NY"}}],"publisher":"Rodopi","dateIssued":"2004","issuance":"monographic"},"language":[{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},{"@objectPart":"translation","languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"ita"}}],"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"354 p. ; 24 cm."},"tableOfContents":"Pt. 1. World of Science and Technology -- Ch. 1. What is Science? -- Ch. 2. Science and Society -- Ch. 3. Is Science Neutral? -- Ch. 4. Science, Technique and Technology -- Ch. 5. Techno-Scientific Ideology -- Ch. 6. Techno-Scientific System -- Pt. 2. Encounter with the Ethical Dimension -- Ch. 7. Norms and Values in Human Action -- Ch. 8. Role of Values in the Human Sciences -- Ch. 9. Theoretical Rationality and Practical Rationality -- Ch. 10. Moral Judgment of Science and Technology -- Ch. 11. Problem of Risk -- Ch. 12. Responsibility of Science in a Systems-Theoretic Approach -- Ch. 13. Ethical Dimension -- Ch. 14. Ethics for Science and Technology -- Commentaries -- Challenge of the Freedom and Responsibility of Science / Juliana Gonzalez -- Full Dimensions of Rationality / Francisco Miro Quesada -- Science, Society and Ethics / Vladislav Lektorsky -- Centrality of Truth / Mario Bunge -- Some Reflections on Agazzi's Philosophy of Science / D. P. Chattopadhyaya -- Practical Rationality and Technical Rationality / Enrico Berti -- Knowledge, Activity and Ethical Judgment / Boris Yudin -- Techno-Sciences and Ethics / Gilbert Hottois -- Alleged Error of Social Epistemology / Paul T. Durbin -- Evandro Agazzi's Ethical Pragmatism of Science / Janos Boros -- Scheme-Interpretationist Sophistication of Agazzi's Systems Approach to Science and Ethics / Hans Lenk -- Note on the Construction of Norms / Jean Ladriere -- Non-Linearity of the Development of Technology and the Techno-Scientific System / Louk Fleischhacker -- Some Questions from the Point of View of an Axiology of Science / Javier Echeverria -- Replies to the Commentaries / Evandro Agazzi.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Evandro Agazzi ; edited by Craig Dilworth."},"\"The present edition differs from all others ... in containing commentaries on the text by leading philosophers of science and of technology, as well as replies to these commentaries by Professor Agazzi\"--P. 10.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Science","Moral and ethical aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Technology","Moral and ethical aspects"]}],"classification":{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"BJ57 .A3513 2004"},"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Poznań studies in the philosophy of the sciences and the humanities ; v. 81. Monographs-in-debate"}},{"@type":"series","titleInfo":{"title":"Poznań studies in the philosophy of the sciences and the humanities","partName":"Monographs-in-debate"}},{"@type":"series","titleInfo":{"title":"Poznań studies in the philosophy of the sciences and the humanities v. 81"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990093297990203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9042009195"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"54514724"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"Soc 715.19 vol. 81"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Widener"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990093297990203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"009329799"}},"processingDate":"2024-08-15T05:12Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@auth